# CTT: rename the Telit LE910Q1 cellular network interface to a stable name "mdm0".
# Covers the ECM composition (1bc7:7021, cdc_ether — the current data path) and the
# legacy RNDIS composition (1bc7:7020, rndis_host — seen only transiently on a modem
# still being migrated to ECM).
#
# Why: the modem netdev otherwise lands as ethN (RNDIS) or wwanN (ECM) and can race
# the USB wired-LAN dongle for eth0/eth1, or land on a name downstream config does
# not key on. Renaming it to mdm0:
#   - keeps `wired-con` ([match] interface-name=eth*) matching only real Ethernet
#     dongles, so the wired LAN name stays deterministic;
#   - gives ModemManager / NetworkManager / the /modem/ppp check a single fixed
#     interface name regardless of composition or enumeration order.
#
# VERIFY ON REBOOT: `ip -br link` shows `mdm0` (not ethN/wwanN) and the wired dongle
# keeps its eth slot. udev net renames can interact with systemd .link policies; the
# image ships empty 73-usb-net-by-mac.link / 99-default.link, so this NAME assignment
# should win — but confirm live.
#
# The netdev add event is ALSO the runtime-recovery trigger for the data path.
# mdm0 is created fresh on every modem re-enumeration (spontaneous modem reset, or
# a re-authorize after disable-modem.sh), and the new interface has no address and
# no route. Nothing used to re-run the bring-up, so a modem that re-enumerated at
# runtime left the station cellular-attached but IP-dead until someone rebooted it
# — see investigations/2026-08-27 (V30B0154C65F, ~22 h offline).
#
# systemd's own 99-systemd.rules already applies TAG+="systemd" and SYSTEMD_ALIAS to
# every net device, so SYSTEMD_WANTS here is sufficient — no extra tagging needed.
#
# Exactly one of the two units below runs per add event; their ConditionPathExists
# on /etc/ctt/modem-disabled are exact complements:
#   marker ABSENT  -> ctt-modem-ecm-up.service      (configure the data path)
#   marker PRESENT -> ctt-modem-reassert-off.service (re-apply the operator's OFF
#                     intent: `authorized` resets to 1 on re-enumeration, so a
#                     disabled modem would otherwise silently come back on the bus)
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1bc7", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7021", NAME="mdm0", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ctt-modem-ecm-up.service", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ctt-modem-reassert-off.service"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1bc7", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7020", NAME="mdm0", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ctt-modem-ecm-up.service", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ctt-modem-reassert-off.service"
